  "policyBody": "Updated: March 4, 2026\n\n1) Purpose and legal basis\nEducational use only. Processing is based on explicit consent (GDPR Art. 6(1)(a) and, where applicable, Art. 9(2)(a)).\n\n2) Data minimization\nLive camera only. No gallery/file intake. Temporary photos are deleted on a best-effort basis. Data-minimization and purpose-limitation principles are applied (GDPR Art. 5 and Art. 25).\n\n3) Profiling limits\nDo not use this app for hiring, credit, insurance, legal or high-impact decisions. No decision should be made solely on this automated output (GDPR Art. 22).\n\n4) Third-party processing\nFree mode uses ad SDKs. Pro unlock uses store billing. Providers may process device/transaction identifiers.\n\n5) Transparency\nUsers are informed that they are interacting with AI-generated content (AI Act Art. 50 transparency principle).\n\n6) Prohibited-use boundaries\nThe app must not be used for manipulative or harmful social-scoring-like uses (AI Act Art. 5 prohibited practices).\n\n7) User rights\nUsers can withdraw consent at any time from this panel. Information duties and rights should be reflected in store-facing privacy notice (GDPR Art. 13 and Arts. 15-17).\n\n8) Medical disclaimer\nNo medical or clinical diagnosis is provided. A red result indicates potential risk markers, not a confirmed disorder.\n\n9) Compliance note\nThis in-app text is not legal advice. Complete legal review before public release.",
